From f00c1c9384ed98c4806b81cbaeceb0baf83b2a32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SkillBuddy Agent <agent@skillbuddy.local>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 21:07:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Android startup crash: remove unused react-native-maps
 dependency
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause confirmed by inspection: react-native-maps was only referenced
in one file, components/ExploreMap.native.tsx — and that file was never
imported anywhere in the app (dead code, no screen used it). Despite
being unused in JS, react-native-maps is still a native dependency that
gets auto-linked into the Android build, and since no Google Maps API
key was configured in app.json, Google Play Services fails to initialize
the Maps SDK at app startup, crashing the app before any screen loads
(not just when a map screen is opened — this matches builds crashing
immediately on launch).

Rather than setting up a Google Cloud account/API key/billing for a
feature that isn't actually used, removed the dependency and the
orphaned file entirely. Lockfile updated (pnpm install: -2 packages).

Requires a new EAS build (native dependency change, not an OTA-eligible
JS change) —  again
after applying this patch.

Full typecheck: zero errors.
---
